Z||000006||theogre||01-12-2001||07:50 PM||||If the car had a miss then you've likely fried the coil. read the article on DIS in my cave. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Cave</A><P>The book is screwed up..... The oil filter is in the bottom of the oil pan. The drawing shows a FWD car. ignore it. You may need a special wrench to get the thing apart without damaging the "plug." You can get one at most autoparts stores. It wasn't very expensive whan I last saw one. Pep Boys had it in with the rest of the filter wrenches on the sales floor.||||reg||1
